>> title: Nixtamalised Masa
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: corn, masa, tortilla, mexican, dough, make-ahead
>> counters: Panadería, Taquería
>> aka: masa, masa nixtamalizada, nixtamalized masa, nixtamal, masa fresca, fresh masa, hominy dough
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, carnitas
>> servings: 12
>> time: 9 hr 15 min
>> slack: unforgiving — cal is caustic and the batch is the batch: under-steeped corn will not give up its hulls, over-steeped goes to slippery mush
>> step.1: slake the cal
>> step.2: simmer the corn 15 min
>> step.3: steep 8 hr
>> step.4: rinse and rub the hulls off
>> step.5: grind to a masa, rest 30 min

Stir @pickling lime{1%tsp}(5 g) into @water for the cook{2%qt}(1.9 L) in a #stockpot{} until the water clouds.

Add @dried field corn{1%lb}(450 g; dent or cacahuazintle) to @&(~1)lime water{}, bring it up and ~simmer{15%min}, stirring now and then, until the tip of a kernel slips its skin when you pinch it.

Cover @&(~1)corn{}, take it off the heat and ~steep{8%hr} overnight.

Drain @&(~1)nixtamal{} and rinse it under @cool water{2%qt}(1.9 L), rubbing handfuls between your palms until the hulls float off and the water runs clear.

Grind @&(~1)rinsed nixtamal{} with @water for the grind{1/2%cup}(120 mL) through a #mill{}, or in batches in a food processor, to a dough that holds a thumbprint without cracking, then ~rest{30%min} to hydrate.
